  "result": "I added `split(cents, parts)` to `shop/money.py`. It gives each part `cents // parts`, and the first `cents % parts` parts get one extra cent, so `split(10, 3)` returns `[4, 3, 3]`. If `parts` is below 1 it raises `ValueError`.\n\nThe tests are in a new `tests/test_money.py`, since there was no money test file yet. I followed the `unittest` style of `tests/test_pricing.py`. They cover:\n- an even split\n- a split with a remainder\n- `parts=1`\n- `parts` of 0 and -1 raising `ValueError`\n- the result always summing to `cents` with exactly `parts` items, for cents 0\u201349 and parts 1\u20137\n\nI ran the full suite with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .` (the command from the README): all 11 tests passed. Nothing is committed.",
